<h1>Identity and access</h1>
<p>Map an authenticated chat subject to a principal, then grant an agent and its capabilities separately.</p>
<p>For a first installation, the <a href="{{ starter }}">Slack GitHub reviewer recipe ↗</a> gives an owner and colleague read-only PR tools in one channel. Its optional owner publishing grant is disabled by default.</p>
</header>
<nav class="guide-jumps" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#profiles">Reviewer profiles</a><a href="#identity">Caller mapping</a><a href="#policy">Worked decision</a><a href="#spaces">Channel scope</a><a href="#constraints">Execution limits</a><a href="#credentials">Credentials</a>
</nav>
<section id="profiles">
<h2>Two reviewers share a read-only group</h2>
<p>Define trust profiles with <code>principals.&lt;name&gt;.groups</code> and Cedar rules. There is no <code>profiles</code> key. For example, this broker excerpt assigns the owner and colleague to <code>pr-reviewers</code> and maps the review channel separately:</p>
<pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Reviewer principal groups"><code>principals:
  owner:
    subjects: [slack.t0123abc.uownerid]
    groups: [pr-reviewers]
  colleague:
    subjects: [slack.t0123abc.ucolleagueid]
    groups: [pr-reviewers]
  review-room:
    subjects: [slack.t0123abc.c0123abc]</code></pre>
<p>A Cedar rule can match <code>principal in Dekopon::Group::"pr-reviewers"</code>. The complete recipe grants that group and the channel permission to prompt <code>pr-reviewer</code>, plus <code>gh.pull-request.list</code>, <code>gh.pull-request.read</code>, <code>gh.pull-request.diff</code>, <code>gh.pull-request.status</code> and <code>gh.content.read</code>. No default rule permits GitHub writes.</p>
<p>The separate <a href="{{ starter }}#optional-owner-review-comments">owner publishing opt-in ↗</a> adds only the owner to <code>pr-publishers</code>, adds <code>gh.pull-request.comment</code>, and gives the channel the matching grant. It also needs the matching HTTP constraints and a PAT with the required PR write permission. It permits a <code>COMMENT</code> review; approval, request-changes, push and merge remain ungranted. The colleague retains read-only access. Once enabled, the owner's grant allows writes without a per-review human approval gate.</p>
<p>Both Slack users act through the broker's configured GitHub PAT. This delegates the owner's repository access; Dekopon doesn't check a separate GitHub login for each Slack user. Collected traces can identify the Slack sender, while GitHub records the PAT account.</p>
</section>
<section id="identity">
<h2>The broker maps the sender, not the prompt.</h2>
<figure class="ownership-map">
<div class="map-input"><strong>Chat service → gateway UID 65533</strong>
<p>The gateway verifies service identity and sends a canonical subject, agent and conversation claim.</p>
</div>
<div class="map-zone broker-zone">
<h3>Broker-owned identity configuration</h3>
<p>Socket peer UID → configured attestor → namespace grant</p>
<p>Attested subject → <code>principals</code> → Cedar principal</p>
<p>Cedar receives principal, action, resource and broker-built context—not a principal selected by the model.</p>
</div>
<figcaption>The socket authenticates the local process separately from the chat identity assertion. The chart’s broker probes use UID 65532, not the gateway identity.</figcaption>
</figure>
